{"step_index":293,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T00:10:58Z","thinking":"The structure of the search results page appears identifiable. The primary search results are encapsulated within a specific HTML `div` with a unique class. Sidebar content, like ads or recent companies, is segregated within another `div` element. The parsing strategy will therefore involve splitting the page content based on this distinct HTML structure. This approach will be tested within the function that handles search page parsing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import re\\n\\nwith open(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\cc5f8116-f40f-4d66-a990-d85efe7bc64f\\\\scratch\\\\bizno_search_snippet.html\\\", \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n    html = f.read()\\n\\ndef parse_main_posts(html):\\n    if '<div class=\\\"col-lg-4 sidebar\\\">' in html:\\n        main_content = html.split('<div class=\\\"col-lg-4 sidebar\\\">')[0]\\n    else:\\n        main_content = html\\n        \\n    posts = re.findall(r'<div class=\\\"single-post[\\\\s\\\\S]*?(?=<div class=\\\"single-post|<hr>|$)', main_content)\\n    results = []\\n    for p in posts:\\n        art_match = re.search(r'href=[\\\"\\\\']/article/(\\\\d{10})[\\\"\\\\']', p)\\n        if not art_match: continue\\n        art_id = art_match.group(1)\\n        \\n        title_match = re.search(r'<h[34][^>]*>(.*?)</h[34]>', p)\\n        title = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', title_match.group(1)).strip() if title_match else \\\"\\\"\\n        \\n        p_match = re.search(r'<p>([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)</p>', p)\\n        addr_snip = re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', p_match.group(1))).strip() if p_match else \\\"\\\"\\n        \\n        results.append({\\n            \\\"biz_no_10\\\": art_id,\\n            \\\"title\\\": title,\\n            \\\"addr_snip\\\": addr_snip\\n        })\\n    return results\\n\\nres = parse_main_posts(html)\\nprint(\\\"Parsed main posts:\\\", len(res))\\nfor r in res:\\n    print(\\\"  ->\\\", r)\\n\"","Description":"\"Test clean post parsing\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\cc5f8116-f40f-4d66-a990-d85efe7bc64f\\\\scratch\\\\test_clean_posts.py\"","toolAction":"\"Testing clean post parsing\"","toolSummary":"\"Test main post parsing\""}}]}
